Subject: libgcc: register i386-substrate with full crt extra_parts

Two-part change to libgcc/config.host:

1. A *-*-substrate* OS-level stanza that sets extra_parts to the
   standard crtbegin.o / crtbeginS.o / crtbeginT.o / crtend.o /
   crtendS.o set (same as Linux), pulls t-crtstuff-pic + t-libgcc-pic
   + t-eh-dw2-dip, and registers t-slibgcc + the GNU ld helpers.
   Without this stanza extra_parts stays empty and gcc's
   STARTFILE_SPEC reference to crtbegin.o fails the link.

2. A per-CPU i[34567]86-*-substrate* stanza that adds i386/t-crtstuff
   (CRTSTUFF_T_CFLAGS for the i386 frame-pointer requirement) and
   pulls in i386/elf-lib.h.  t-dfprules enables decimal-floating-
   point ops in libgcc.  No md_unwind_header yet — C++ exceptions
   that roll out of signal handlers will not work until one is
   provided.

---
diff --git a/libgcc/config.host b/libgcc/config.host
--- a/libgcc/config.host	2026-05-11 23:07:26.175151480 -0500
+++ b/libgcc/config.host	2026-05-11 23:58:51.509691315 -0500
@@ -297,6 +297,14 @@
   tmake_file="$tmake_file t-crtstuff-pic t-libgcc-pic t-eh-dw2-dip t-slibgcc t-slibgcc-fuchsia"
   extra_parts="crtbegin.o crtend.o"
   ;;
+*-*-substrate*)
+  # Same set as linux: full crtbegin/end + the S (shared) and T
+  # (static) flavours.  t-crtstuff-pic builds PIC versions of the
+  # support code; t-libgcc-pic builds libgcc itself PIC so it can
+  # be linked into shared objects.
+  tmake_file="$tmake_file t-crtstuff-pic t-libgcc-pic t-eh-dw2-dip t-slibgcc t-slibgcc-gld t-slibgcc-elf-ver"
+  extra_parts="crtbegin.o crtbeginS.o crtbeginT.o crtend.o crtendS.o"
+  ;;
 *-*-linux* | frv-*-*linux* | *-*-kfreebsd*-gnu | *-*-gnu* | *-*-kopensolaris*-gnu | *-*-uclinuxfdpiceabi)
   tmake_file="$tmake_file t-crtstuff-pic t-libgcc-pic t-eh-dw2-dip t-slibgcc t-slibgcc-gld t-slibgcc-elf-ver t-linux"
   extra_parts="crtbegin.o crtbeginS.o crtbeginT.o crtend.o crtendS.o"
@@ -783,6 +791,14 @@
 	;;
 x86_64-*-openbsd*)
 	;;
+i[34567]86-*-substrate*)
+	# Substrate builds standard i386 ELF libgcc.  No unwind header
+	# yet (signal handlers don't reach into libgcc's unwinder),
+	# no t-heap-trampoline (no GCC nested-function support needed
+	# for the libraries we actually build).
+	tmake_file="${tmake_file} i386/t-crtstuff t-dfprules"
+	tm_file="${tm_file} i386/elf-lib.h"
+	;;
 i[34567]86-*-linux*)
 	extra_parts="$extra_parts crtprec32.o crtprec64.o crtprec80.o crtfastmath.o"
 	tmake_file="${tmake_file} i386/t-crtpc t-crtfm i386/t-crtstuff t-dfprules"
